# nr-tui-app-run: the application state, the picker wiring, the boot sequence, the event loop and the teardown of mixdog-tui

Fills `mixdog_tui::app` (`app.rs`, `app/*.rs`) and `mixdog_tui::run` (`run.rs`), and adds `tests/app_state.rs`. Nothing in it was
compiled by its author (no cargo in the task); the lead compiles it with the wave. The syntax of every file was parsed with
`rustfmt --check`; types and traits were checked by reading.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

`crates/mixdog-tui/Cargo.toml` gains `[dev-dependencies]`: `portable-pty`, `vte`, `tempfile`, `mixdog-cli`, `mixdog-core` (all
`workspace = true`, all already in `[workspace.dependencies]`), and the features `rt`, `rt-multi-thread`, `sync` on its `tokio`
dependency. The lock file needs the new edges `mixdog-tui -> portable-pty, vte, tempfile, mixdog-cli, mixdog-core`
(`cargo metadata --offline --locked` will say). `mixdog-workspace-hack` and the workspace `Cargo.toml`: no change.

## Protocol rows, SERVICE_PENDING, registrations

None. Nothing is added to or removed from `SERVICE_PENDING`. The store calls the application makes are the Node store's: `getTheme`,
`setTheme` (the first two stay local, see below), `touchProjectSelected`, `setEffort`, `getOnboardingStatus`, `getProviderSetup`,
`listProviderModels`, `listWebSearchModels`, `listAgents`, `getDisabledSkills`, `getUsageDashboard`, `askSide`, `cancelSide`,
`completeOAuthProviderLogin`, `getOAuthProviderLoginStatus`, plus every call the pickers and the slash dispatch make.

## What the application now is (interfaces added)

* `app::AppState` owns the panel surface (`PanelSurface<AppPicker, ContextPanel, Value>`), the prompt state, the exit flow, the
  catalog caches, the onboarding and provider-flow state, the settings controller, the extension pickers, the `/btw` controller and
  the frame inputs. It implements, once each: `AppCtx`, `SlashHost`, the model `PickerHost`, the settings `PickerHost`,
  `ProviderHost` + `ModelLabels`, `ExtensionsHost`, `PanelsHost` and `BtwHost`. `AppCtx` gained `run_action(AppAction)` (default:
  nothing): a continuation (`returnTo`, the wizard's Next/Back/Cancel) names its target instead of closing over it.
* `app::picker::AppPicker` is the one picker type: `Model(PickerPanel)`, `Settings(Panel)`, `Provider(ProviderPanel)`,
  `Ext(ExtPanel)`, `Slash(SlashPanel)` (the `slash-loading:<command>` frame and the `/stop` confirmation).
* `app::store::AppStore` is the store the application calls (blocking); `SessionStoreIo` is its one implementation over
  `mixdog_session_view::store::SessionStore` and the tokio runtime that serves it.
* `AppState::mount()` (first mount: the project list as the first frame's picker when the session is empty and the wizard does not
  own the screen), `run_background()` (the project list read, the disabled-skill read, the wizard's launch, catalog refresh jobs,
  the wizard's prefetch, the `/usage` read, the boot catalog warm-up after `PREFETCH_DELAY_MS`, one item per call),
  `on_timers()`, `next_deadline()`, `on_state_published()`, `on_store_event()`, `on_ui_open_request()`, `exit_step()`,
  `dispose_settled()`, `picker_input(input, key)`, `render_frame(columns, rows)`, `theme_epoch()`.
* `run::run_tui(TuiOptions)` is the boot sequence, the loop and the teardown; `TuiOptions` gained `tool_mode`, `remote`,
  `force_onboarding`, `worktree`, `resume` (the options of `runTui`). The switch task (`nr-tui-switch`) calls it.

## Decisions the lead should know

* The three theme methods stay in this process (`bindLocalThemeMethods`): `listThemes`, `getTheme` and `setTheme` are answered by
  `mixdog_tui_style::theme`; `setTheme` mirrors the switch to the core with the caller's `persist` (the core writes `ui.theme`
  for `persist: true`, and only bumps its epoch otherwise). The persisted theme is read with `getTheme` from the core after the
  connection: reading the config file before the connection needs a lane proof (`mixdog-fsio`), which the terminal UI does not have.
* `SlashHost::open` is `AppState::open_now`: JSON options name their targets (`returnTo: "settings"` and the like are turned
  into `AppAction::Open`); an open that arrives while the extension pickers are mid-call is queued and runs when the call returns.
  A continuation that a picker hands to the provider setup (`ProviderSetupRequest::on_continue`) is held and addressed by id
  (`Callback::Open(Opener::Model, {"continuation": id})`).
* `AppStore::has_method` answers true for every name: `mixdog-session-view` does not export the router's table of targets, so a
  method the core lacks answers with the call's own `Err` instead of the silent `null` of Node's `store.name?.()`. Exporting
  `has_action(name)` from `mixdog-session-view` would restore it.
* `pushNotice(text, tone, { ttlMs })` is delivered without the ttl (the session store's `push_notice` has none).

## Not wired by this task (see the result's notDone)

The prompt box types and submits (`app::prompt`: the editor, `slash::on_submit`, so slash commands and `/quit` work), and the picker
keys reach the picker on screen. Not connected to the loop yet: the prompt handlers (`PromptHost`: history, paste, interrupt,
queue restore, the slash palette, double Esc) and the key handler before them (`GlobalKeyHost`: tool approval keys, copy-first
Ctrl+C, panel Escapes, paging), the keys of the text-entry prompts (API key, OAuth code), the mouse handler (`MouseHost`), the
transcript scroll engine (`ScrollHost`), the footer (`StatusHost`/`StatusIo` and its schedule), the spinner row, the tool approval
and question panels, the welcome hint, and the `Interrupt` of a running turn.
